00:00:00.264 --> 00:00:02.847
(upbeat music)

00:00:07.047 --> 00:00:08.933
- Hi, I'm Hannah, you're
friendly neighborhood wine mom.

00:00:08.933 --> 00:00:11.656
Tonight we're drinking some
red wine in a mini bottle

00:00:11.656 --> 00:00:14.534
that's really fancy 'cause
it has a twig tied onto it.

00:00:14.534 --> 00:00:16.067
There was a comment on a previous video

00:00:16.067 --> 00:00:18.051
asking what's the worst parenting advice

00:00:18.051 --> 00:00:19.921
I've ever gotten, and that's pretty funny,

00:00:19.921 --> 00:00:21.842
so I figured I'd tell
you guys the three worst

00:00:21.842 --> 00:00:24.507
pieces of parenting advice
I've ever gotten in my life.

00:00:24.507 --> 00:00:28.101
So let's go right into it, after a sip.

00:00:28.101 --> 00:00:30.249
First, sleep when the baby's sleeping,

00:00:30.249 --> 00:00:33.134
and I know so many moms
get this piece of advice.

00:00:33.134 --> 00:00:35.060
It just makes no sense.

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:37.761
Should I do laundry when
the baby's doing laundry?

00:00:37.761 --> 00:00:39.374
Should I pee when the baby's peeing?

00:00:39.374 --> 00:00:41.703
Should I do dishes when
the baby's doing dishes?

00:00:41.703 --> 00:00:43.926
I'll just take a long nap
while the baby's sleeping,

00:00:43.926 --> 00:00:46.149
and do the rest while they're
helping me out with it,

00:00:46.149 --> 00:00:48.512
because that works out just great.

00:00:48.512 --> 00:00:51.077
When the baby is sleeping
is what I like to call

00:00:51.077 --> 00:00:52.720
get shit done time.

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:54.972
That's when I do everything I couldn't do

00:00:54.972 --> 00:00:55.970
with a baby in my arms.

00:00:55.970 --> 00:00:57.722
Try vacuuming with a baby in your arms,

00:00:57.722 --> 00:00:59.274
and they're scared of the vacuum.

00:00:59.274 --> 00:01:01.120
They're not cooperative people.

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:03.087
So instead of sleep when the baby sleeps,

00:01:03.087 --> 00:01:05.160
how about you volunteer to come clean

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:06.225
while the mommy sleeps?

00:01:06.225 --> 00:01:09.168
I think that's a better
piece of parenting advice.

00:01:09.168 --> 00:01:11.536
Next, I get gold all the
time that holding you child

00:01:11.536 --> 00:01:13.418
too much will spoil them.

00:01:13.418 --> 00:01:14.908
I don't think it's possible for your child

00:01:14.908 --> 00:01:17.096
to get spoiled off of physical contact.

00:01:17.096 --> 00:01:19.236
I'm pretty sure the only
thing that's gonna spoil them

00:01:19.236 --> 00:01:22.449
is giving them too much
stuff that's undeserved

00:01:22.449 --> 00:01:24.074
and letting them get away with being

00:01:24.074 --> 00:01:25.935
a jerk without consequences.

00:01:25.935 --> 00:01:28.385
The whole point of a parent
is to care for and comfort

00:01:28.385 --> 00:01:31.101
your child, so if I'm not
picking them up when they

00:01:31.101 --> 00:01:34.103
wanna be held, what am I here for?

00:01:34.103 --> 00:01:35.966
Me picking up my child when they're hurt

00:01:35.966 --> 00:01:38.705
or sad or feeling bad
is only gonna make them

00:01:38.705 --> 00:01:40.913
feel more secure with
themselves and therefore

00:01:40.913 --> 00:01:42.817
be a better person.

00:01:42.817 --> 00:01:44.546
I feel like this advice comes from a time

00:01:44.546 --> 00:01:46.851
when parents were a lot more
distant from their kids,

00:01:46.851 --> 00:01:49.276
and it was kind of like I
don't wanna deal with that.

00:01:49.276 --> 00:01:52.064
And now we're in a time where
parents wanna deal with that.

00:01:52.064 --> 00:01:53.747
I want to be there for my children.

00:01:53.747 --> 00:01:56.307
I want to be their source of comfort.

00:01:56.307 --> 00:01:59.724
So to give me that advice is nonsensical.

00:02:00.614 --> 00:02:02.861
And last, people say that
you should teach your kids

00:02:02.861 --> 00:02:06.390
to use non-anatomical words
for their private parts.

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:08.959
They think you should make up like a more

00:02:08.959 --> 00:02:11.431
kid-friendly word for it, like oh my gosh,

00:02:11.431 --> 00:02:12.884
I hurt my wee wee.

00:02:12.884 --> 00:02:14.817
That's just super weird.

00:02:14.817 --> 00:02:17.395
My friend's daughter got
sent home from school

00:02:17.395 --> 00:02:20.465
with a note asking her to
stop telling her daughter

00:02:20.465 --> 00:02:24.036
to say vagina and instead
to say down there.

00:02:24.036 --> 00:02:26.880
That's just so weird
because, to me, down there

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:28.964
means anything from
the waist down, so like

00:02:28.964 --> 00:02:33.775
when I say down there, I could
mean legs, shins, feet, toes.

00:02:33.775 --> 00:02:35.501
When you use the actual word about it,

00:02:35.501 --> 00:02:37.039
it clears up all the mystery.

00:02:37.039 --> 00:02:39.307
It's not this foreign
thing that you can't say

00:02:39.307 --> 00:02:41.160
the actual word, like Voldemort.

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:43.552
Everyone in Harry Potter's
like, my God, don't say

00:02:43.552 --> 00:02:47.350
Voldemort, but when you
actually say it, it's like,

00:02:47.350 --> 00:02:48.445
oh, that's who he is.

00:02:48.445 --> 00:02:50.894
That being said, I was
raised with the idea

00:02:50.894 --> 00:02:53.753
of not saying anatomically correct words,

00:02:53.753 --> 00:02:56.336
and to this day, I get
extremely uncomfortable

00:02:56.336 --> 00:03:00.419
using the words penis (laughing)

00:03:11.139 --> 00:03:12.631
I'm an adult.

00:03:12.631 --> 00:03:14.668
I'm gonna teach my kids the correct way

00:03:14.668 --> 00:03:16.410
to say their privates.

00:03:16.410 --> 00:03:17.842
That's just how it's gonna be.

00:03:17.842 --> 00:03:19.003
Penis. (laughing)

00:03:19.003 --> 00:03:20.205
That's all I've got for today.

00:03:20.205 --> 00:03:22.161
I'm Hannah, your friendly
neighborhood wine mom,

00:03:22.161 --> 00:03:24.530
and if you've received a worse
piece of parenting advice,

00:03:24.530 --> 00:03:26.853
leave it in the comments,
because I gotta see it.

00:03:26.853 --> 00:03:28.743
In the meantime, I gotta get on Facebook

00:03:28.743 --> 00:03:31.323
and start telling other people
how to raise their kids,

00:03:31.323 --> 00:03:33.976
because it's really important
to do that as a parent.

00:03:33.976 --> 00:03:35.226
Till next time.

